  "notes": "Stanford second-life release (OSF qsabn): hash-named cycling workbooks for six cells. It shares cell ids G1, V4, V5 with dataset_27. Landing page (osf.io/qsabn) not fetched: the OSF project is private, so the API node lookup returns 401 for every anonymous request; confirmed by manually visiting the URL, which requires login. Cell spec (INR21700-M50T) from LG's INR21700 M50 18.2Wh document, the same source used for dataset_27. Charge/discharge rate estimates, where explicitly marked raw_data in the citations, use signed observed current extrema divided by the stored nominal Ah. These are measurement estimates over the cached extraction scope, not imposed CC protocol setpoints; they may include pulse, dynamic, regenerative or diagnostic segments and measurement excursions. Current units and direction were checked against the cited original headers, status labels or separate charge/discharge counters. cached extraction covers six recognised cells and parsed workbooks, including diagnostic parts; 2077 lock markers remain, so coverage is the available parsed local delivery. stored nominal capacity 5.0 Ah comes from the nearest LG M50 datasheet, not an independently matched exact M50T sheet. The witness workbook Global_Info Capacity field is 4.85, and its 14.55 A charge plateau is consistent with its CC_3C label using that author denominator. The proposal uses the stored 5.0 Ah denominator as requested. CC_3C in this workbook's filename accompanies positive charging segments 7/8, rather than establishing a discharge C-rate. The existing 0.5C discharge scalar obtained by assigning CC filename tokens to discharge is unsupported and should be replaced. Finite auxiliary temperature readings exist, but the sensor placement on the cell versus ambient air was not established; measured cell-temperature availability is therefore unclear."
 },
